// Deep groove ball bearing 625, 5 x 16 x 5 mm, shielded on both faces:
// the outer and inner steel rings and the shields between them. Its axis
// along z, a face at z = 0, centered on the origin.
// https://kramp.com/shop-de/en/p/deep-groove-ball-bearing-5x16x5mm-skf--625SKF
//
// From SKF's figures for the 625, as Kramp lists them: 5 x 16 x 5 mm, dynamic
// load rating 1140 N, static 380 N, 4.7 g.
// The bore, outside diameter and width are ISO 15's for the designation,
// so any maker's 625 has them. The rings' section and the shields are
// drawn, not measured. To hold it in a printed part, `bearing_seat.c2f`
// cuts its pocket.

// @description Deep groove ball bearing 625, 5 mm bore, 16 mm outside, 5 mm
// @description wide: for a 5 mm shaft, as a NEMA 17 motor's, in a small
// @description printed mechanism.
// @spec bearing: deep groove ball bearing, single row, 625 (SKF 625)
// @spec bore: 5 mm
// @spec outside diameter: 16 mm
// @spec width: 5 mm
// @spec dynamic load: 1.14 kN
// @spec static load: 0.38 kN
// @spec mass: 4.7 g
// @source https://kramp.com/shop-de/en/p/deep-groove-ball-bearing-5x16x5mm-skf--625SKF SKF 625 at Kramp (dimensions, load ratings, mass)

use <lib/ball_bearing.c2f>

module bearing_625() {
    ball_bearing(5, 16, 5);
}

bearing_625();
